 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch37_04_01\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idm190917760\" data-alt=\"The hypothalamus secretes thyrotropin-releasing hormone, which causes the anterior pituitary gland to secrete thyroid-stimulating hormone. Thyroid-stimulating hormone causes the thyroid gland to secrete the thyroid hormones T3 and T4, which increase metabolism, resulting in growth and development. In a negative feedback loop, T3 and T4 inhibit hormone secretion by the hypothalamus and pituitary, terminating the signal.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20241024.164013/resources/574107daaac72faebf16f0f3b53297f929af9815\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"The hypothalamus secretes thyrotropin-releasing hormone, which causes the anterior pituitary gland to secrete thyroid-stimulating hormone. Thyroid-stimulating hormone causes the thyroid gland to secrete the thyroid hormones T3 and T4, which increase metabolism, resulting in growth and development. In a negative feedback loop, T3 and T4 inhibit hormone secretion by the hypothalamus and pituitary, terminating the signal.\" width=\"280\" height=\"373\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 546628,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Terry recently gained weight and has been more tired than usual. Terry’s doctor suggested that he might not produce enough thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH). Evaluate the diagram to justify the doctor's claim by explaining why a TSH deficiency could cause Terry’s weight gain and fatigue.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1071658,
     "content_html": "Without TSH, there would be excessive production of T3 and T4, leading to a high metabolic rate that would cause weight gain and fatigue."
    },
    {
     "id": 1071659,
     "content_html": "Without TSH, there would be excessive production of T3 and T4, leading to a low metabolic rate that would cause weight gain and fatigue."
    },
    {
     "id": 1071660,
     "content_html": "Without TSH, T3 and T4 cannot be properly produced, leading to a high metabolic rate that would cause weight gain and fatigue."
    },
    {
     "id": 1071661,
     "content_html": "Without TSH, T3 and T4 cannot be properly produced, leading to a low metabolic rate that would cause weight gain and fatigue."
    }
   ],
